s and each staff member’s own permissions also apply.\n\nDelegated administrationCo-managed SLA priorities\nCustomer-approved access\n\nOversight of the initial service desk board\n\nBoards\n\nService Desk: Collaborate\n\nProjects\nStaff\nQA Tester\nAccess for QA Tester\nCollaborate\nRemove\nSearch\nSelect an item\nSelect...\nAdd\nTeams\n\nNo access configured.\n\nSearch\nSelect an item\nSelect...\nAdd\nSave access\nReload current access\nCo-managed SLA priorities\n\nMap customer priorities to MSP priorities. New escalations use your client, board, or default SLA policy. Existing clocks keep their targets.\n\nCM isolated SLA 1792945862860\nManage SLA policies\nMSP priority for Low\nNot mapped\nMSP priority for Critical\nP1 - Critical\nMSP priority for Medium\nNot mapped\nMSP priority for High\nNot mapped\nMSP priority for Urgent\nNot mapped\nSave access\nReload current access\nDelegated administration\n\nCustomer-approved assistance with selected settings and user records.\n\nRefresh access\nCustomer workspace: CM DESK 1792935726307 Accept IT · MSP: Oz\n\nNo administration tasks are currently approved.\n\nShared tickets\nFilters\nView\n\n0 tickets · 0 open · 0 closed\n\nNo customer tickets to show yet.\n\nOpen in Customer Tickets\nWork\n\nClient projects and shared task queues stay in the MSP shell with their qualified identities.\n\nProjects\nProject task queues\nEnd co-management\n\nReview what happens when this relationship ends.\n\nCM DESK 1792935726307 Accept IT\n\nLive access between these organizations ends immediately when you confirm.\n\nThe customer keeps its workspace and data. Read access, export, and upgrade to an independent AlgaPSA subscription remain available.\n\nThe MSP retains its own records and permitted historical evidence of shared work it participated in.\n\nAllocated co-managed seats return to the MSP’s pool. This does not cancel subscriptions or delete either workspace.\n\nReview departureRefresh status",
